  "description": "This is a no-foolin' racing bike, a serious, dedicated\n\ntime trial or triathlon bike. That such bikes exist is not a surprise. That\n\none so competitive and well outfitted exists at this price level is flat amazing.\n\nThis is no converted road bike. It was a wind-cheating rocket-ship from the\n\nfirst dot on the drawing board.\n\nWheels? Fast rolling 650s, 24 bladed spokes in front, 28 in back. Deep-V Velocity\n\nrims, UltraLite tubes, Michelin Axial Pro tires. Fast wheels.\n\nThe frame? Kinesis Aero aluminum, 7005 Series alloy, double-butted. The hanger for the rear derailleur is detachable, replaceable\n\nwhen the airline drops your bike box on the way to Hawaii. Fork's a Kinesis,\n\ntoo, alloy and aero.\n\nScan the specs. Note the expensive Speedplay X-4 pedals, the rare and pricey\n\nShimano Dura-Ace 9-speed bar-ends, the Profile Split Second/Air Wing handlebars.\n\nSerious parts. Serious frame. Serious bike. Aloha.",
